# Atlas secrets
#
# Setup: copy this file to `.env` in the repository root and fill in the keys below.
# `.env` is gitignored and is loaded at startup WITHOUT overriding variables already set in
# your shell. NEVER commit a real .env file. Every value here is empty on purpose.
#
# Everything that is not a secret (concurrency, retries, database path, host, port, log
# level, ...) lives in ONE place: src/configs/config.yaml. The AI providers, models, fallback
# order and LLM API keys are managed in the app (Models and Keys pages), stored in the database.
# A missing key does not stop Atlas from starting; the Diagnostics screen
# (GET /api/diagnostics) reports what is missing.

# The YouTube key accepts several values separated by commas (or YOUTUBE_API_KEY_2=..., _3=...
# lines); Atlas rotates through them and skips a key that is out of quota or rejected. Quotas
# are per Google Cloud project, so use keys from DIFFERENT projects for extra capacity.
#
# REQUIRED to ingest playlists: YouTube Data API v3 key (Google Cloud Console, enable
# "YouTube Data API v3"). Without it POST /api/playlists answers 503 CONFIG_MISSING.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# LLM keys below are a FIRST-RUN IMPORT ONLY. On the first start after the model registry
# migration (0007) Atlas copies any key set here into the Keys page; after that these variables are
# ignored, so add, change and remove LLM keys on the Keys page. Leave them empty if you prefer to
# enter keys in the app. Keys are stored in the database unencrypted (data/atlas.sqlite3 is
# gitignored; keep it private). Each accepts several comma-separated values, and numbered extras
# (GEMINI_API_KEY_2=...) are imported too.
# Gemini (Google AI Studio) API key.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OpenRouter API key.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# FreeLLMAPI gateway key (OpenAI-compatible, default http://localhost:3001/v1).
FREELLMAPI_API_KEY=
# NVIDIA NIM key (https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1).
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
# Any other provider: add its key and model on the Keys and Models pages. See docs/CONFIG.md.

# Google Drive publishing does not use a key here: upload the OAuth client file on the
# Settings page (or save it as credentials.json) and complete the consent flow once. The
# resulting token.json grants Drive access: never commit it (both files are gitignored).

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: one-off overrides of config.yaml (prefer editing config.yaml)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any config.yaml setting can be overridden as ATLAS_<SETTING_IN_UPPERCASE>, for example:
#   ATLAS_PORT=8001
#   ATLAS_MAX_CONCURRENT_VIDEOS=3
#   ATLAS_DATABASE_PATH=D:/atlas-data/atlas.sqlite3
#   ATLAS_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG
# The prompt file setting also accepts the short name NOTES_PROMPT_NAME. Empty values count as
# unset. (The old NOTES_PROVIDER / GEMINI_MODEL / ... names are gone: models are chosen on the
# Models page.)
# An invalid value stops startup with a message naming it.
